course: dictionary
lesson: 14242
title: Needs and wants
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A necessity is something you need and cannot do without. Water is a necessity, because you cannot live for long without it. A want is something nice to have, but you can live without it. Sorting things into needs and wants is an important skill.
explain: «Mum packed food, water and a warm coat, because they were necessities on the long hike.» The clues are food, water and a warm coat. These are things you must have, so a necessity is something you really need.
explain: The word also has a plural, necessities, which means the basic things needed to live, such as food and shelter. You will also meet the phrase «out of necessity», which means someone had to do something because there was no other choice. «The farmer sold a cow out of necessity, because there was no money left for food.»
fact: A necessity is something you need and cannot do without.
fact: «Necessity» can also mean the fact of being needed, as in «the necessity of sleep».
fact: «Necessities» (plural) means the basic things needed to live, such as food and shelter.
fact: «Out of necessity» means because you have no other choice.
fact: A want is nice to have, but you can live without it; a luxury is something extra and special.
exercise: Which of these is a necessity? | A new pair of trainers | *Clean water to drink | A toy robot | A bag of sweets
exercise: «The farmer sold a cow out of necessity, because there was no money left for food.» What does out of necessity mean here? | In a hurry to get home | *Because there was no other choice | By accident | For fun
exercise: Which two of these are basic necessities? | *Food and shelter | Food and a video game | A video game and a bike | Shelter and a video game
test: «The children learned that water and food are necessities, but a new bike is a want.» What is the difference between a necessity and a want? | *A necessity is needed to live; a want is nice but not needed | They mean exactly the same thing | A necessity is nice to have; a want is needed to live | Wants are always cheaper than necessities
test: In the saying «Necessity is the mother of invention», what does it mean? | *People invent things when they really need them | Inventions are always cheap to make | Mothers are the best inventors | People never invent anything at all
exam: «The necessity of sleep is clear: a tired child cannot learn well.» What does the necessity of sleep mean? | A dislike of going to bed | A long and boring night | A soft bed in a fancy room | *The fact that sleep is needed
